{
  "summary": "Adds an optional build-time script evaluation tracer exposed via the libbitcoinkernel C API and its C++ wrapper. When compiled with `-DENABLE_SCRIPT_TRACE=ON`, macro hooks in `EvalScript` dispatch execution state frames (begin, step, end) to a registered global callback on every opcode evaluation. In non-tracing builds, the hooks compile to no-op stubs with zero runtime overhead.",
  "problem": "External applications using libbitcoinkernel cannot inspect intermediate script execution state step-by-step, making it impossible to build script debuggers or fine-grained execution analyzers on top of the library. In addition, interpreter unit tests and fuzzing cannot easily observe whether intermediate script states are correct before a subsequent error condition shadows faulty behavior.",
  "evidence": [
    "The PR author implemented a proof-of-concept debugger targeting rust-bitcoinkernel demonstrating the trace API in practice (PR description).",
    "The author cites PR #33961 as an example where script interpreter bugs were obscured because unexpected behavior was shadowed by a later error condition (PR description)."
  ],
