  "scope_notes": "Touches core consensus validation code in `src/script/interpreter.cpp` by inserting `SCRIPT_TRACE_SCOPE` and `SCRIPT_TRACE_STEP` macro invocations into `EvalScript`. By default, `ENABLE_SCRIPT_TRACE` is turned off and the macros evaluate to `static_assert(true)`.",
  "changed_since_previous": "No substantial changes to the implementation architecture or scope; the patch remains a single commit introducing the CMake option, interpreter trace macros, C/C++ bitcoinkernel wrapper APIs, and unit tests.",
  "card": "Adds an optional build-time script evaluation tracer exposed through the libbitcoinkernel C API and C++ wrapper. External consumers currently cannot inspect intermediate interpreter execution steps to construct script debuggers or execution analyzers. The author implemented a proof-of-concept debugger using rust-bitcoinkernel to demonstrate the interface, and highlights potential testing and fuzzing benefits to prevent errors from shadowing interpreter defects. The feature is disabled by default via CMake and requires no prerequisite PRs.",
